# Triton JIT-compiles vLLM's kernels at run time and needs a compiler for its
# launcher stubs; without one the engine core dies before it registers.
#
# BOTH compilers, not just gcc. The launcher Triton builds is C++, so it invokes
# g++ — with only gcc present the image looks right, vLLM starts, and then the
# engine dies and the pod answers 502. Found the hard way on an olmOCR pod: the
# TLS problem was fixed, the pod became reachable, and the next layer underneath
# was a missing g++.
gcc
g++
libc6-dev
